silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_04_shared_diagram_concrete_anchor a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "SharedDiagramConcreteAnchorExample" .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_04_shared_diagram_concrete_anchor silm:hasExample "In 'SharedDiagramConcreteAnchor', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, F_source: the source view functor that renders the Mittens cocone claim as the witnesses.csv ledger rows listing VetRecord_77, MicrochipID_44, DomesticCat, FelisCatusTSN183798, and the nine remaining typed legs; also, kappa: the comparison map from colim(F_v circ D_Mittens) to F_v(MittensColimitApex) for each view v; for the multi-view agreement law, kappa must be an isomorphism for each view; also, DenseClaimExample: the twelve-leg cocone theorem in 02_mittens_anchor is the canonical dense claim that requires all four synchronized views; the VetRecord_77 table, the tikzcd diagram, the plain-English summary, and the witnesses.csv rows are its four synchronized views." .
